Falsifies `periodic_deadline::proofs::nothing_on_the_beat_is_skipped_between_now_and_the_answer`.

The defect: a second period is added after the snap, which is what someone writes who reads
`now - r` as the *next* occurrence rather than the last one and then adds a period to get past
it. The answer is still on the beat, still strictly after `now`, and still at least a period on
from `prev`, so it fails none of the other three proofs in this file.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!(next - period <= now)`, for any `now` off the beat,
where the returned fire has a whole occurrence sitting between `now` and itself: exactly the
skipped tick this proof exists to rule out.

diff --git a/crates/periodic_deadline/src/lib.rs b/crates/periodic_deadline/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/periodic_deadline/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/periodic_deadline/src/lib.rs
@@ -454,3 +454,3 @@ pub const fn next_after(prev: u64, period: u64, now: u64) -> u64 {
     let r = (now - prev) % period;
-    (now - r).saturating_add(period)
+    (now - r).saturating_add(period).saturating_add(period)
 }
